      "provenance": "literature_retrieved",
      "rationale": "L4 states the HA tag was introduced between the signal peptide and the N-terminus of full-length Shisa9. The topology landmarks place the signal peptide at residues 1\u201323 and the mature N-terminus at residue 24; the junction is therefore after residue 23 (A) and before residue 24 (Q), confirmed by reading the numbered sequence. After SP cleavage the HA tag becomes the new extracellular N-terminus of the mature protein, 128 residues from the TM boundary. L5 from the same paper confirms the tagged construct is expressed and functional in co-IP assays. Full-length HA-tagged Shisa9 construct with the HA tag introduced between the signal peptide and the N-terminus of the mature protein. Expressed in HEK293T cells and used for co-immunoprecipitation with V5-tagged interactors using anti-HA antibody, validating expression and protein\u2013protein interaction of the tagged full-length construct.",
